@title EPISODE 29 • VALENTINE'S DAY
@bg penthouse_day
February 14th. London is on the couch with an ice pack and a terrible attitude.
@show paris
Paris: Jayden's taking me to dinner. Are you going to be okay?
London: I'm going to be extremely okay. Alone. Eating truffle fries. As planned.
Doorbell. Paris answers it and gasps.
@show diggy
Diggy is standing there in the too-short blazer, holding an envelope.
Diggy: Before anything else. This is for your dad. Every dollar. Took me since December. Double shifts at Casa Morales. Cassie covered my Sundays so I could pick up more.
London: Diggy, he doesn't want it back. He told you that.
Diggy: I know. I don't want it to be the reason. If we're doing this, I want it to be clean. Just you and me. Nobody's money.
> [Sweet] "...You did all that for me?" -> v1
> [Bitchy] "You're so dramatic. Come inside." -> v2
> [Bold] "Then ask me properly." -> v3
> [Good] "I'll give it to him. Together. At spring break." -> v4
*v1
@add Diggy_Trust 4
@add Diggy_Affection 3
Diggy: Did it for me too. I needed to look your dad in the eye one day.
@jump v_done
*v2
@add Diggy_Affection 3
Diggy: (stepping in, grinning) I learned from the best.
@jump v_done
*v3
@add Diggy_Affection 4
@add London_Confidence 2
Diggy: (dropping to one knee — Paris SCREAMS — "Not like THAT, Paris!") London Sterling. Will you go on one real date with me? No relays, no Cassie, no money.
@jump v_done
